==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|unwasched}}, {{m|enm|unwasschyd}}, {{m|enm|unwessched}}, a [[weak verb]] conjugation of earlier {{der|en|enm|unwaschen|t=[[unwashen]]}}, equivalent to {{af|en|un-|washed}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɒʃt|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not having been [[wash]]ed.
#: {{syn|en|unwashen|q1=obsolete}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Abbot|volume=I|page=85|passage=I say that the eyass should have her meat '''unwashed''', until she becomes a brancher—’twere the ready way to give her the frounce, to wash her meat sooner, and so knows every one who knows a gled from a falcon.}}
# [[vulgar|Vulgar]], [[plebeian]], [[lowbrow]]. {{rfex|en}}
#* {{RQ:Oakley Hall|title=Warlock|passage=Gannon is looked upon with distrust by a good many members of the Citizens’ Committee—or perhaps it is with jealousy. He remains, however, a hero to the unwashed elements.}}

